 "nudge_why": {
  "tax_official": "sits on the bench behind the desk (bench at D 12.9-13.2); his feet are hidden in the painting",
  "rail watchers": "legs hidden behind the railing: stand 0.3 m behind the near railing's inner face so the elbows rest on its top rail (lean_chin keeps the feet under the hips); bridge_sightseer steps off the post at X 3.5, and watchers 3 and 4 stand 0.8 m apart so their elbows don't meet",
  "wall_recliner": "half-reclining against the foot of the gate block's east face, as painted; his estimated foot maps 0.7 m north of the block's north end (the block is literal, 9 m along the wall), so he moves 1.2 m south onto the face, and 1.1 m east to lean on it",
  "tower_watchman": "painted in the middle of the hall doorway (bay X -21.05..-19.15); now that people have bodies he would block the way in, so he stands 0.6 m to the side of it",
  "barber_7805": "crouches over the recliner, so he moves with him (1.07 m east, 1.2 m south)",
  "far rail": "far-railing figures stand 0.42 m south of the far railing's inner face so they can lean on its top rail (their feet are hidden behind it in the painting)",
  "rail_leaner_8665": "as the near-rail watchers: 0.39 m north of the near railing",
  "far_figure_8205": "stands 0.5 m in front of the far shed's posts (his foot is painted against them)",
  "distant_figures": "the two distant marks are 0.14 m apart on the map; each steps 0.3 m aside so their bodies do not overlap",
  "hat_pole_man_5940": "painted at the corner of the low building, leaning forward toward the viewer; that way runs into the house within a step, so he steps 0.7 m off the corner and walks along the street toward the gate and back",
  "caravan_leader_7388": "painted on the lead camel's far (north) side in the passage, where the 2.4 m passage has no room for him beside the camel and a walker: he stands just outside the mouth on that side, at the camel's head, facing out of the city (he leads it; the camel stands, so he does too)",
  "cast_2026_10_12": "recast with the workshop's new characters (2026-10-12): the archers are the archer (one draws his bow, one binds his wrist); the beggar boys and the small figure are the child (holding out their hands); the old rider is the elder sitting side-saddle; the veiled rider the hat traveller; the carriers walk with their painted loads on the porter's shoulder-pole walk (bundles, baskets) and the back-box porter under his boxes; the 串车's two carters push it where it stands and the groom holds the donkey's bridle (the cart and the donkey stand, so they do too); the man with the long pole and board holds his pole upright"
 },
